#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508069 :question/problem "Determine $\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nLet's attempt to evaluate the limit approaching $(1,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Taking $x\\to (1,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 1}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Taking $x\\to (1,0)$ along the path $x=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)\\,\\,\\,x=1}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\lim_{y\\to 0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\lim_{y\\to 0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{y\\to 0}1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508171 :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3a-3b &=-18 \\\\ -2a+b &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=7+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-3b & =-18 \\\\ 3a-3(7+2a) & =-18 \\\\ 3a-21-6a & =-18 \\\\ -3a-21 & =-18 \\\\ -3a & =3 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=7+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7+2(-1) \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(5)=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508174 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y &=21 \\\\ y &=x-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.The solution is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$, $\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $y:$\n\n$$\ny=x-3\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $y$ in the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =21 \\\\ x+5(x-3) & =21 \\\\ x+5x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =36 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=6$ into $y=x-3,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(6)-3 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508179 :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b &=2 \\\\ -3a+b &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =8 \\\\ b & =8+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=8+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b & =2 \\\\ -3a-2(8+3a) & =2 \\\\ -3a-16-6a & =2 \\\\ -9a-16 & =2 \\\\ -9a & =18 \\\\ a & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-2$ into $b=8+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =8+3(-2) \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-2-(2)=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508187 :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y &=2 \\\\ 3x+y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-5-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-5-3x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+3y & =2 \\\\ 3x+3(-5-3x) & =2 \\\\ 3x-15-9x & =2 \\\\ -6x-15 & =2 \\\\ -6x & =17 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{17}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{17}{6}$ into $y=-5-3x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-3\\left(-\\frac{17}{6}\\right) \\\\ y & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{17}{6},\\,y=\\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508204 :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y &=8 \\\\ -2x+y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ y & =6+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=6+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y & =8 \\\\ -3x+4(6+2x) & =8 \\\\ -3x+24+8x & =8 \\\\ 5x+24 & =8 \\\\ 5x & =-16 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{16}{5}$ into $y=6+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6+2\\left(-\\frac{16}{5}\\right) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{16}{5},\\,y=-\\frac{2}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508205 :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b &=9 \\\\ -3a+b &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =3 \\\\ b & =3+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=3+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b & =9 \\\\ -5a+2(3+3a) & =9 \\\\ -5a+6+6a & =9 \\\\ a+6 & =9 \\\\ a & =3 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=3$ into $b=3+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =3+3(3) \\\\ b & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=3-(12)=-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508207 :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4p &=-24 \\\\ p+5q &=19\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-6$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =19 \\\\ (-6)+5q & =19 \\\\ 5q & =25 \\\\ q & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=-6-(5)=-11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508210 :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b &=6 \\\\ -4a+b &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4a+b & =-7 \\\\ b & =-7+4a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-7+4a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b & =6 \\\\ -3a-3(-7+4a) & =6 \\\\ -3a+21-12a & =6 \\\\ -15a+21 & =6 \\\\ -15a & =-15 \\\\ a & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=1$ into $b=-7+4a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-7+4(1) \\\\ b & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=1-(-3)=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508214 :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ satisfy $b=135-11a.$\n\nThe coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $7b+162a=435.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=135-11a \\\\ 7b+162a &=435\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=135-11a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7b+162a & =435 \\\\ 7(135-11a)+162a & =435 \\\\ 945-77a+162a & =435 \\\\ 945+85a & =435 \\\\ 85a & =-510 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=135-11a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =135-11(-6) \\\\ b & =201\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=201.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508215 :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2a-4b &=-14 \\\\ -2a+b &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =6 \\\\ b & =6+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=6+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a-4b & =-14 \\\\ -2a-4(6+2a) & =-14 \\\\ -2a-24-8a & =-14 \\\\ -10a-24 & =-14 \\\\ -10a & =10 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=6+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =6+2(-1) \\\\ b & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(4)=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508227 :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y &=5 \\\\ 2x+y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y & =-1 \\\\ y & =-1-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-1-2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y & =5 \\\\ 5x-2(-1-2x) & =5 \\\\ 5x+2+4x & =5 \\\\ 9x+2 & =5 \\\\ 9x & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=-1-2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1-2\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508233 :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y &=12 \\\\ -2x+y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =5 \\\\ y & =5+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=5+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =12 \\\\ 2x+2(5+2x) & =12 \\\\ 2x+10+4x & =12 \\\\ 6x+10 & =12 \\\\ 6x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=5+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5+2\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ y & =\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=\\frac{17}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508977 :question/problem "Given that $q(x,y)=xy,$ find $\\frac{∂q}{∂\\theta },$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $q(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta ,$ where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂q}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂q}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂q}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂q}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $q$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂x}=y,\\,\\frac{∂q}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂x} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂q}{∂y} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂\\theta } & =-(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509348 :question/problem "Find $2a-2b+4c$ if $a=7i+7j$, $b=-9i-5j$, and $c=-7i+9j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $2a-2b+4c,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a-2b+4c &= 2(7i+7j) - 2(-9i-5j) + 4(-7i+9j) \\\\\n&= 14i + 14j + 18i + 10j - 28i + 36j \\\\\n&= (14i + 18i - 28i) + (14j + 10j + 36j) \\\\\n&= 4i + 60j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509350 :question/problem "Find $3a + b$ if $a = -8i - 5j$ and $b = -5i - 4j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $3a+b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a+b &= 3(-8i-5j) + (-5i-4j) \\\\\n&= -24i - 15j - 5i - 4j \\\\\n&= (-24i - 5i) + (-15j - 4j) \\\\\n&= -29i - 19j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509352 :question/problem "Find $3a-3(b-(-3c))$ if $a=-6i+j$, $b=-5i-2j$, and $c=-2i-j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $3a-3(b-(-3c)),$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a-3(b-(-3c)) &= 3(-6i+j)-3((-5i-2j)-(-3)(-2i-j)) \\\\\n&= 3(-6i+j)-3(-11i-5j) \\\\\n&= -18i + 3j + 15i + 6j + 18i + 9j \\\\\n&= (-18i + 15i + 18i) + (3j + 6j + 9j) \\\\\n&= 15i + 18j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509354 :question/problem "Find $a+2b$ if $a=-6i-j$ and $b=-6i+5j.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $a+2b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(-6i-j)+2(-6i+5j) \\\\  & =-6i-j-12i+10j \\\\  & =(-6i-12i)+(-j+10j) \\\\  & =-18i+9j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509362 :question/problem "Find $3a+2b$ if $a=4i-8j$ and $b=12i-7j.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $3a+2b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2b & =3(4i-8j)+2(12i-7j) \\\\  & =12i-24j+24i-14j \\\\  & =(12i+24i)+(-24j-14j) \\\\  & =36i-38j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509365 :question/problem "Find $3a-3(b-2c)$ if $a=2i+2j$, $b=-6i-4j$, and $c=-5i+3j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $3a-3(b-2c),$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a-3(b-2c) &= 3(2i+2j)-3((-6i-4j)-2(-5i+3j)) \\\\\n&= 3(2i+2j)-3(4i-10j) \\\\\n&= 6i + 6j + 18i + 12j - 30i + 18j \\\\\n&= (6i + 18i - 30i) + (6j + 12j + 18j) \\\\\n&= -6i + 36j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509384 :question/problem "Find $2a-3(b-2c)$ if $a=-3i-j$, $b=-3i+3j$, and $c=5i+6j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $2a-3(b-2c),$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a-3(b-2c) &= 2(-3i-j)-3((-3i+3j)-2(5i+6j)) \\\\\n&= 2(-3i-j)-3(-13i-9j) \\\\\n&= -6i - 2j + 9i - 9j + 30i + 36j \\\\\n&= (-6i + 9i + 30i) + (-2j - 9j + 36j) \\\\\n&= 33i + 25j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509387 :question/problem "Find $-3a+4b+2c$ if $a=-4i-8j$, $b=9i-5j$, and $c=8i-7j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $-3a+4b+2c,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a+4b+2c &= -3(-4i-8j) + 4(9i-5j) + 2(8i-7j) \\\\\n&= 12i + 24j + 36i - 20j + 16i - 14j \\\\\n&= (12i + 36i + 16i) + (24j - 20j - 14j) \\\\\n&= 64i - 10j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509400 :question/problem "Find $-2a-4b-3c$ if $a=7i-5j$, $b=-4i+3j$, and $c=i-7j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $-2a-4b-3c,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a-4b-3c &= -2(7i-5j) - 4(-4i+3j) - 3(i-7j) \\\\\n&= -14i + 10j + 16i - 12j - 3i + 21j \\\\\n&= (-14i + 16i - 3i) + (10j - 12j + 21j) \\\\\n&= -i + 19j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509403 :question/problem "Find $3a+3b+4c$ if $a=-5i-2j$, $b=-2i-j$, and $c=2i+3j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $3a+3b+4c,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a+3b+4c &= 3(-5i-2j) + 3(-2i-j) + 4(2i+3j) \\\\\n&= -15i - 6j - 6i - 3j + 8i + 12j \\\\\n&= (-15i - 6i + 8i) + (-6j - 3j + 12j) \\\\\n&= -13i + 3j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509430 :question/problem "Find $-2a-4b+4c$ if $a=-3i+3j$, $b=-3i+8j$, and $c=3i+j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $-2a-4b+4c,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a-4b+4c &= -2(-3i+3j) - 4(-3i+8j) + 4(3i+j) \\\\\n&= 6i - 6j + 12i - 32j + 12i + 4j \\\\\n&= (6i + 12i + 12i) + (-6j - 32j + 4j) \\\\\n&= 30i - 34j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509432 :question/problem "Find $a-2b$ if $a=-7i-11j$ and $b=8i+6j.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $a-2b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-2b & =(-7i-11j)-2(8i+6j) \\\\  & =-7i-11j-16i-12j \\\\  & =(-7i-16i)+(-11j-12j) \\\\  & =-23i-23j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509435 :question/problem "Find $2a+3b$ if $a=4i+4j$ and $b=-12i-8j.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $2a+3b,$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b & =2(4i+4j)+3(-12i-8j) \\\\  & =8i+8j-36i-24j \\\\  & =(8i-36i)+(8j-24j) \\\\  & =-28i-16j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509440 :question/problem "Find $-3a-2(b-3c)$ if $a=-4i-6j$, $b=4i+3j$, and $c=6i-4j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $-3a-2(b-3c),$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a-2(b-3c) &= -3(-4i-6j)-2((4i+3j)-3(6i-4j)) \\\\\n&= -3(-4i-6j)-2(-14i+15j) \\\\\n&= 12i + 18j - 8i - 6j + 36i - 24j \\\\\n&= (12i - 8i + 36i) + (18j - 6j - 24j) \\\\\n&= 40i - 12j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509449 :question/problem "Find $-2a-2(b-(-3c))$ if $a=-6i-4j$, $b=-i-3j$, and $c=3i-j$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $-2a-2(b-(-3c)),$ we just need to compute all of the $i$'s and $j$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a-2(b-(-3c)) &= -2(-6i-4j)-2((-i-3j)-(-3)(3i-j)) \\\\\n&= -2(-6i-4j)-2(8i-6j) \\\\\n&= 12i + 8j + 2i + 6j - 18i + 6j \\\\\n&= (12i + 2i - 18i) + (8j + 6j + 6j) \\\\\n&= -4i + 20j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509456 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $3a - ((-4)b + 2c)$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a - ((-4)b + 2c) &= 3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-((-4)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}40 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509457 :question/problem "Let $$\n\\displaystyle a=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle c=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ Find $a+(4b-4c).$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+(4b-4c) & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+(4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}-32 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -40\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -33\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509465 :question/problem "Let $$\n\\displaystyle a=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle c=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ Find $3a+(2b-(-5)c).$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+(2b-(-5)c) & =3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+(2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}-(-5)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -48\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -60\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509478 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a+3b$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na+3b &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509482 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a+4b$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na+4b &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509497 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a - (4b + 4c)$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - (4b + 4c) &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}-(4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}32 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}60 \\\\ -40\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-55 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509504 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a - (3b + 5c)$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - (3b + 5c) &= \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-(3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509512 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $5a - (5b + (-3)c)$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5a - (5b + (-3)c) &= 5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-(5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+(-3)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}23 \\\\ -22\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509527 :question/problem "Let $$\n\\displaystyle a=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle c=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ Find $(-3)a-((-3)b+3c).$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)a-((-3)b+3c) & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-((-3)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-21 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-21 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-21 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509536 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a+5b$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na+5b &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}40 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}46 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509544 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a+2b$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na+2b &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
